WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.202
That's a burbot.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.236
Holy.

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.137
Look, Maya.

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:05.405
I got it?

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:07.140
Yeah, you got it.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.609
Maya was able to pull out a
lush, which was a big deal.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.177
Because it's a
different kind of fish.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.379
None of my kids ever seen one.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.580
I've never caught one.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.315
And I was really proud
of her to be able to pull

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.050
in a nice lush like that.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:19.419
Feels good to get a burbot.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:22.489
My first time ever catching
one, first time with the kids.

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:23.390
They're excited.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.591
I'm excited.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:27.394
Did she see little
Maya pull it out?

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.962
That's golden.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:31.131
I can't believe
we got a burbot.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:32.198
That's so cool.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:34.300
We still have more
lines to check, too.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.268
Oh, yeah.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:48.281
Well, there's a fish on it.

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.182
Holy.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:50.383
That's a big pike.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.719
That's a huge pike.

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:53.620
Dang.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.255
Ooh.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:58.224
Oh, that's a big pike.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.125
It's dead.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.160
Huge.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.761
Eee.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:04.230
I have a good
lever inside of it.

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:07.600
Let me show you the other one.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.568
Pull it in, then.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:09.502
You got another one?

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:10.403
Yep.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.337
Oh, it's still alive.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:12.238
Burbot.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.173
Come on, burbot.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:13.740
Burbot.

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:14.574
Come on, burbot.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.141
[inaudible]

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.276
It's a burbot.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.177
Burbot.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.178
Man, it's a huge one.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:18.812
Look at it.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:19.712
Oh.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.682
That's a big one.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.417
Huge, huh?

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.685
Yeah, and now we can eat--

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:26.986
OK, so we got--

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:27.887
--two ones.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.189
Oh, oh, oh.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.391
It's like a big snake.

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:33.593
Gee.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.694
Stand right here.

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:37.597
Let's see how big
it is next to you.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:38.998
Its tail is on the ground.

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:39.899
[laughs]

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.000
It's big is you, Maimai.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.402
Uh.

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:44.904
OK, we're going to
make a little fire

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.873
and cook some
burbot, have a feast.

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.415
It's definitely a
different-looking fish.

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:56.916
See how like, the
flakes are bigger.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.985
Oh, yeah.

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.453
Oh, look at those moose.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.989
A baby [inaudible].

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.524
Yeah, a baby moose.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.525
Oh, oh.

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:08.628
Hey, it listened to her.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:09.829
Oh, oh.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:10.396
It listened to you.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:11.764
Oh.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.766
Holy, Maya, you're going to
be hunting moose pretty soon.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:19.005
That's the beauty of having
kids, and being in the woods,

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.240
and being happy out here.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.308
It's just part of being with
nature and part of being

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:25.278
with your culture is learning
to enjoy yourselves while you're

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:27.380
getting food on the table.

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:30.517
My hands are so tired,
they're shaking.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.417
[inaudible]

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.385
More.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:33.386
Mmm, mmm, mmm, mmm, mmm, mmm.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.254
It's good.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.288
You have another one, Mai?

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.256
Yeah.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:40.960
Jeez, that fish is gone quick.

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:42.562
That was so [inaudible].

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:43.463
It was?

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.364
No more.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.199
That was good, huh?

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.667
Mm-hmm.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.669
I just want to fall
back and go to sleep.

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.604
Me too.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:52.772
[inaudible]

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:53.673
Good.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.208
Good job, Maya.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.175
Good job fishing.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:56.809
[inaudible]

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:57.677
All right, there.

